@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law, Schedule A1, Part D — "גיל הזכאות לקצבת אזרח ותיק לנשים לפי חודש לידתן", the
-- age of entitlement to a senior citizen pension for women, by month of birth. Row IL-08.
-- Source lines 4431-4453.
--
-- GAPS.md item 10 of row IL-07: s 342(c)(2) stops the employer's deduction "after the insured reaches
-- 70 for a man, and for a woman the age fixed for her, by her month of birth, in Part D of Schedule
-- A1"; row IL-05 takes that age as an input in months, and the capstone declined a woman for whom it
-- was not given. This module gives it.
--
-- The schedule's own note (line 4432) lists where Part D is used: ss 245(a), 342(c), 351(b) and
-- 406(a)(4)(a). The table is encoded as the text prints it, and its answer is the age in months, the
-- unit row IL-05 takes (65 years and 4 months is 784).
--
-- THE TABLE AS IN FORCE AT RETRIEVAL. Part D's heading carries the tag תשע״ז־12 and the Part the tag
-- תש״ף; no rule here takes a date, and the table is stated as the deposited text prints it. Its last
-- row is open ("May 1950 and after: 70"), so every woman born from May 1950 on has the age of 70.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Schedule A1, Part D — the age of entitlement for women, by month of birth`

-- src:4431 | ⟦ח:קטע3|לוח א1 חלק ד|חלק ד׳⟧
-- src:4432 | ⟦ח:קטע4||[note: (סעיפים 245(א), 342(ג), 351(ב) ו־406(א)(4)(א))]|תיקון: תש״ף⟧
-- src:4433 | ⟦ח:קטע4||גיל הזכאות לקצבת אזרח ותיק לנשים לפי חודש לידתן|תיקון: תשע״ז־12⟧
-- src:4437 | חודש הלידה גיל הזכאות (בשנים)
-- src:4438 | עד יוני 1939 65
-- src:4439 | יולי ואוגוסט 1939 65 ו־4 חודשים
-- src:4440 | ספטמבר 1939 עד אפריל 1940 65 ו־8 חודשים
-- src:4441 | מאי עד דצמבר 1940 66
-- src:4442 | ינואר עד אוגוסט 1941 66 ו־4 חודשים
-- src:4443 | ספטמבר 1941 עד אפריל 1942 66 ו־8 חודשים
-- src:4444 | מאי 1942 עד דצמבר 1944 67
-- src:4445 | ינואר עד אוגוסט 1945 67 ו־4 חודשים
-- src:4446 | ספטמבר 1945 עד אפריל 1946 67 ו־8 חודשים
-- src:4447 | מאי עד דצמבר 1946 68
-- src:4448 | ינואר עד אוגוסט 1947 68 ו־4 חודשים
-- src:4449 | ספטמבר 1947 עד אפריל 1948 68 ו־8 חודשים
-- src:4450 | מאי עד דצמבר 1948 69
-- src:4451 | ינואר עד אוגוסט 1949 69 ו־4 חודשים
-- src:4452 | ספטמבר 1949 עד אפריל 1950 69 ו־8 חודשים
-- src:4453 | מאי 1950 ואילך 70

-- A calendar month as one count: twelve times the year plus the month less one.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` TIMES 12 PLUS `the month` MINUS 1

-- The table, row by row in the source's order, as "born in or before the last month of the row".
-- Ages in years and months as printed, then in months. Typed from the rows quoted above and
-- checked edge by edge in the tests module against them.
--                                                                   to month          age      in months
@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4435-4452
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 6  `of` 1939 THEN 780   -- to June 1939: 65
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1939 THEN 784   -- July and August 1939: 65 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1940 THEN 788   -- September 1939 to April 1940: 65 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1940 THEN 792   -- May to December 1940: 66
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1941 THEN 796   -- January to August 1941: 66 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1942 THEN 800   -- September 1941 to April 1942: 66 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1944 THEN 804   -- May 1942 to December 1944: 67
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1945 THEN 808   -- January to August 1945: 67 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1946 THEN 812   -- September 1945 to April 1946: 67 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1946 THEN 816   -- May to December 1946: 68
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1947 THEN 820   -- January to August 1947: 68 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1948 THEN 824   -- September 1947 to April 1948: 68 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1948 THEN 828   -- May to December 1948: 69
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1949 THEN 832   -- January to August 1949: 69 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1950 THEN 836   -- September 1949 to April 1950: 69 and 8 months
        OTHERWISE                                                840   -- May 1950 and after: 70
    WHERE `born` MEANS `the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year`

@export The age, in months, that Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law fixes for a woman by her month of birth (the age s 342(c)(2) and s 245(a) read for women)
@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4431-4453
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE  @desc the woman's date of birth; only its month and year are read
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` (DATE_MONTH `the date of birth`) `of` (DATE_YEAR `the date of birth`)

§§ `The day she reaches the age (fork N4; version 0.3.0)`

-- The day she reaches it: her date of birth moved on by that many months. Where the later month has
-- that day of the month, it is that day, whatever the reading. Where it lacks it (born on the 31st and
-- reaching the age in a 30-day month, born on 29 February and reaching it in a common year's
-- February, born on the 29th to 31st and reaching it in February), Part D does not say which day she
-- reaches it (fork N4, inventory item DATE). Three readings are kept by name (nouns, `A reading of
-- Part D of Schedule A1 where the day she reaches the age does not exist`): the last day of the
-- shorter month (`add months` clamps; this row's reading in versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, as row IL-05's
-- fork F19); the 1st of the next month; such a day is declined. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG,
-- BACKLOG IL-41): declined by default, this row's rule being to decline where the text does not
-- decide. The switch is the rule below; the other readings are a one-line change there.
@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4431-4453 (an age in years and months, no day); fork N4; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of Part D of Schedule A1 where the day she reaches the age does not exist`
`Schedule A1, Part D — the reading this row takes where the day she reaches the age does not exist` MEANS
    `Part D: such a day is declined`

@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4431-4453; fork N4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth` MEANS
    REFUSE "Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"

-- `add months` gives the same day of the month where it exists, and the last day of the month where
-- it does not; so the day is missing exactly when the day of the month it gives differs from hers.
@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4431-4453; fork N4
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      r                   IS A `A reading of Part D of Schedule A1 where the day she reaches the age does not exist`
GIVETH A DATE
`Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` `the date of birth` `, reading a day the month lacks as` r MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month` EQUALS DATE_DAY `the date of birth`
    THEN `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month`
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `Part D: the last day of the shorter month` THEN `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month`
         WHEN `Part D: the 1st of the next month`         THEN `add months` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month`) (DATE_YEAR `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month`)) 1
         WHEN `Part D: such a day is declined`            THEN `Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth`
    WHERE
        `the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month` MEANS
            `add months` `the date of birth` (`Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` `the date of birth`)

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref NII Schedule A1, Part D, lines 4431-4453; the switch above
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` `the date of birth`
        `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Schedule A1, Part D — the reading this row takes where the day she reaches the age does not exist`
